\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item Let  $\lambda=\max_i\{|\lambda_i|, \lambda_i\text{  eigenvalue of  } K\}$. Then, for any $0<\varepsilon\le \min\left\{\frac{1}{(n+1)\lambda}, \frac12\right\}$  there exists a  solution $\hat{u}_{\varepsilon}\in C^\infty(\Omega\setminus\Omega_\text{out})$ of the equation $(*_{\hat{\varepsilon}})$ that is zero on $\partial\Omega$ and blows up to infinity over $\Sigma_\text{out}$,  that is $\lim_{x\to x_0}\hat u_\varepsilon(x)=\infty$ for any $x_0\in \Sigma_\text{out}$.
